=== PRE-EXISTING BUILD-UNBLOCKERS (in allowed files apps/apple/**) ===
================================================================================
The tree did NOT compile for Apple at HEAD — accumulated because every prior
Apple gate was BLOCKED at macOS signing before a clean iOS compile/test was ever
reached. None of these are P9-0002 code; each is the minimal, mechanical fix
needed for the app + UI-test bundle to BUILD so the deliverable can be verified.
Each was driven by the compiler (authoritative), not by heuristics:
  1. #Preview @ViewBuilder `return` (Swift rejects `return` once a #Preview body
     contains @Previewable): removed `return` from 22 @Previewable preview blocks
     in 6 shared-surfaces/*.Previews.swift (Accordion, Checkbox, HelpIcon, Input,
     RangeSlider, SearchInput). Non-@Previewable previews were left untouched
     (their `return` is required — plain `() -> some View` closures).
  2. Input.Previews.swift: 2 InputField(...) calls had placeholder after error/
     hint; reordered to the init's declared order (… placeholder, error, hint …).
  3. DriveScoreModels.swift / DriveScorePage.Panels.swift: String(localized:) was
     passed a LocalizedStringKey (it wants String.LocalizationValue). Added a
     `labelText: String` accessor mirroring `labelKey` and used it at the call site.
  4. GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift (P9-0001 unit): a @MainActor static helper was
     called from a nonisolated stub; marked it `nonisolated` (it only builds a
     value type). This unblocks the unit bundle's COMPILE (its runtime failure is
     a separate pre-existing item below).

